    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Kyle Tucker**, whose 80.93 score is the cream of the crop. Facing the vulnerable arm of Young (xERA 4.79), **Kyle Tucker** is perfectly positioned to capitalize on a favorable wind-out scenario at his venue, mirroring the environment that also elevates **Andy Pages** (75.64) to a elite-tier play. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.84) also grades out as a primary engine today; his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed Martinez, N (xERA 4.63) and a favorable batting order spot at #2 maximize his potential for both counting stats and stolen base opportunities. While **Jackson Merrill** (57.18) sits on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier, he faces a stiffer test against the high-skill Eovaldi; his heavy reliance on stolen bases makes him a volatile, yet necessary, asset in our pursuit of category volume.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Wade Meckler** (52.57). While his favorable park and platoon advantage nearly earned him a starting nod over **Curtis Mead** (59.20), **Curtis Mead** ultimately secured the UTIL spot due to his slightly superior projected efficiency against the Martinez, N matchup. We continue to monitor **Nasim Nunez** (51.42) as a high-upside bench stash; however, his current #9 spot in the lineup drastically limits his run-scoring ceiling for today\u2019s contest, keeping him out of the primary rotation. Owners should note that while **Gunnar Henderson** (67.11) remains a cornerstone, he faces Sheehan, a pitcher with legitimate swing-and-miss stuff; that SP skill variance is the only factor preventing **Gunnar Henderson** from pushing into the 75+ range. Ensure all lineups are finalized, as we remain hyper-vigilant regarding any late-breaking wind shifts or defensive alignment changes that could impact the base projections for **Sam Antonacci** or **Drake Baldwin**.",
